cuems-nodeconf (0.1.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a controller-engine crash-loop introduced by enabling nodeconf: the
    nodeconf responder IPC socket (/tmp/nodeconf.ipc) was created root-owned, so
    the engine (unprivileged cuems user) failed its Communicator R/W access
    check and exited 1 in a restart loop whenever nodeconf won the boot race to
    create the socket first. nodeconf now chmods the socket 0666 right after
    binding the responder, so any local CUEMS process can reach it.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Fri, 12 Jun 2026 12:40:00 +0200

cuems-nodeconf (0.1.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * AliasPublisher: actually pass AVAHI_PUBLISH_NO_REVERSE to AddAddress. 0.1.0-4
    defined the constant but the call still passed flags=0, so the UI alias
    (formitgo.local) kept failing with "Local name collision" on the reverse PTR
    for the address the host already owns via its native hostname record.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:00:00 +0200

cuems-nodeconf (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix three bugs a live controller smoke test surfaced:
    - merge_discovered_nodes now matches discovered services to the map by UUID
      (the stable primary key), not the mac derived from the avahi service name.
      The controller's service is named 'controller', so the name-parse yielded
      a garbage key and every discovery pass DUPLICATED the controller node and
      flipped the real entry to online=False, orphaning role_id/alias/hostname.
    - AliasPublisher publishes the UI alias with AVAHI_PUBLISH_NO_REVERSE so it
      no longer collides with the host's own reverse PTR on the shared address
      (formitgo.local failed with "Local name collision").
    - AsyncCommsThread cancels the engine-listener task and closes its event
      loop on stop(), so pynng frees the nng aio inside the loop instead of at
      interpreter exit, where it panicked (pthread_mutex) and core-dumped on
      every stop/restart.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 11 Jun 2026 21:05:00 +0200

cuems-nodeconf (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: ship ONLY cuemsnodeconf* — strip every other file dh-virtualenv
    stages in the venv bin/ and site-packages. Those (pip/wheel/activate plus
    dependency payloads such as peewee, its standalone pwiz.py module, lxml,
    pynng, dbus, ...) are provided by the cuems-utils venv + python3-* system
    packages and otherwise file-conflict with cuems-utils at dpkg install time
    ("trying to overwrite '.../pwiz.py'"). Blanket strip is robust against new
    stragglers, unlike the previous dep-name allow-list.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 11 Jun 2026 20:40:00 +0200

cuems-nodeconf (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild of the resident-daemon code for first controller deploy. No source
    changes vs the 0.1.0-1 working tree; version bumped so dpkg performs a clean
    upgrade over the stale 0.1.0-1 build found installed on hosts (Dec-2024
    one-shot code) and the deployed build is traceable.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 11 Jun 2026 20:30:00 +0200

cuems-nodeconf (0.1.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging (dh-virtualenv); console entry cuems-nodeconf in
    the shared /usr/lib/cuems venv.
  * Re-enable nodeconf as a long-running daemon: resident avahi discovery loop,
    debounced network_map refresh, atomic + change-detected map writes.
  * Drop removed cuemsutils.daemon.run_daemon; sd_notify READY=1 via a plain
    signal-handled main() (Type=notify compatible).
  * Interface-scoped avahi aliases via D-Bus EntryGroup.AddAddress
    (controller.local on the cluster iface, UI alias on the outward iface);
    skip controller.local when the OS hostname is 'controller'.
  * Fix copy-on-serialize (node_type enum no longer mutated in place),
    remove_service node removal, per-instance listener state, shutil.copy2 for
    the slave template.
  * Drop the stale in-repo network_map.xsd (runtime validates against the
    cuems-common-shipped /etc/cuems/network_map.xsd).

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Thu, 11 Jun 2026 19:49:46 +0200
